    <briefdescription>
<para>Mean unit normal of an OpenFOAM patch and how far its faces deviate from it. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para><ref refid="namespaceNeoN" kindref="compound">NeoN</ref>&apos;s fixedValue carries a single value for the whole patch, so a boundary condition defined per face along the surface normal has to collapse to one normal. <computeroutput><ref refid="structNeoFOAM_1_1detail_1_1PatchNormal_1a7a9446140a550d642976ba37a2c8d6e3" kindref="member">deviation</ref></computeroutput> is the largest |n_f - meanNormal| over the patch faces: 0 on a planar patch (where the collapse is exact), O(1) on a strongly curved one. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
